=== Iteration 3 — 2026-08-19T09:02Z ===
Task: FR-1 (PRD.md §4.1) — unit test for TripManager pickup arrival/departure distance
tracking against real synthetic GPS points, asserting deadhead and delivery-leg distance
match the known path within a tolerance.

Read TripManager's actual pickup-tracking code (_evaluate_pickup, _process_point_during_trip,
_start_trip, add_pickup) directly rather than guessing the API. Key real behavior confirmed
by reading, then exercised by the test:
- gps_points is reset to [] on trip start, so cumulative distance tracking begins fresh from
  whatever GPS point is first fed to on_gps_update() after the trip becomes ACTIVE -- not from
  the point that crossed the start-speed/hold threshold (that point is consumed inside the
  IDLE branch and never reaches _process_point_during_trip).
- Arrival snapshots _deadhead_distance_km = current cumulative distance the moment the
  driver enters the 50m geofence (ARRIVAL_GEOFENCE_METERS) around the pickup coordinates.
- Departure (leaving that geofence again) snapshots _distance_at_departure_km and returns a
  {"restaurant_name", "wait_minutes"} event exactly once.

Wrote app/src/main/python/tests/test_trip_manager_pickup_distance.py: drives a real
Database(":memory:") + TripManager through the actual state machine (speed/hold trip start,
add_pickup, three GPS points along a straight line: pre-arrival -> exactly at pickup ->
~100m past it 72s later) and asserts, against independently-computed expected distances
(via the module's own haversine_meters on the same coordinates -- verifying the
ACCUMULATION/snapshot logic, not re-deriving the haversine formula itself):
- deadhead snapshot matches the real straight-line distance from trip start to pickup,
  within 1 meter
- departure snapshot matches deadhead + the post-arrival leg, within 1 meter
- wait_minutes == 1.2 (72s / 60), within 0.01
- departure distance > deadhead distance (sanity check that state actually advanced)

Command: `python3 -m pytest app/src/main/python/tests/test_trip_manager_pickup_distance.py -v`
Output: 1 passed (test_pickup_arrival_and_departure_distance_tracking)
