Task: FR-7 and FR-8 (PRD.md §4.2) — unit tests covering the 3-tier fallback (restaurant-
specific -> cross-restaurant average -> hardcoded default) for both deadhead distance
estimation and restaurant wait time.

Read _estimate_deadhead_km (reads offer_distance_accuracy, populated elsewhere at trip
persistence time -- inserted directly via SQL for this test since there's no dedicated
"record deadhead" method to call) and _restaurant_wait_info/record_restaurant_wait (has a
real public recording method, used directly).

Wrote app/src/main/python/tests/test_smart_score_deadhead_and_wait.py, 6 tests (3 tiers x 2
factors):
- Deadhead tier 3 (no history anywhere): 0.0 km, 0 samples, not restaurant-specific.
- Deadhead tier 2 (cross-restaurant avg): a restaurant with no history of its own falls back
  to the average of ALL recorded deadhead samples (2.0km, 4.0km -> 3.0km avg, 2 samples).
- Deadhead tier 1 (restaurant-specific): with both Restaurant A's own history (2.0, 4.0 ->
  3.0) AND a very different Restaurant B (100.0) in the DB, A's estimate must use only its
  own average, not blend with B's -- this is the key regression case (a real bug would be
  averaging across all restaurants even when restaurant-specific data exists).
- Same 3 tiers for restaurant wait time (6.0 min default -> cross-restaurant average ->
  restaurant-specific average), using the real record_restaurant_wait() running-average path.

